e "14\\sqrt{29}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122374} {:answer/id #uuid "a8340c19-e527-5c1b-953c-c260766408b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14\\sqrt{21}}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122375} {:answer/id #uuid "db0760d0-b134-5ae3-af68-54c39c2f1781" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10\\sqrt{29}}{29}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122376} {:answer/id #uuid "0801896c-1c2b-510b-86df-c0542a7bf4e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14\\sqrt{29}}{29}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122377}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0801896c-1c2b-510b-86df-c0542a7bf4e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14\\sqrt{29}}{29}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122377} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dfb4078-c321-5580-bb20-9356ac667745" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122372}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ba373e3-c7d5-54ce-a51c-b2950c874b69" :question/math-academy-id "q-36273" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=2x+{y}^{2}$ at the point $(0,1)$ in the direction of the vector $\\mathbf{v}=5\\mathbf{i}+2\\mathbf{j}.$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $v$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)=∇f(a,b)\\cdot u\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is a unit vector in the direction of $v.$\n\nFirst, we find the unit vector $u$ in the direction of $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{2}^{2}}=\\sqrt{29} \\\\ u & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{29}}(5i+2j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x+{y}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x+{y}^{2})\\text{ }j \\\\  & =2\\,i+2y\\,j \\\\ ∇\\,f(0,1) & =2\\,i+(2\\cdot 1)\\,j \\\\  & =2i+2j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{u}^{′}(0,1) & =∇\\,f(0,1)\\cdot u \\\\  & =(2i+2j)\\cdot (\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{29}}i+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{29}}j) \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{29}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14\\sqrt{29}}{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125029 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93fcdd41-5aba-54fd-9f19-d383cd0c8b1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{78}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122775} {:answer/id #uuid "abdb47d5-6a5e-50f3-b8d6-ae7cb6744ce6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122776} {:answer/id #uuid "b32de488-c397-50e7-9e0d-a9d2fa222187" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122777} {:answer/id #uuid "5be9dc56-00c0-5419-8e09-cdc3986dabdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{21}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122778} {:answer/id #uuid "6f19ba24-1488-5e98-a493-56f081245961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{78}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f19ba24-1488-5e98-a493-56f081245961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{78}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122779} :answer-field/id #uuid "52446f3c-8c33-54d6-a7e9-42d22d6cabce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122774}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f655da5c-6e4d-590f-afb2-3ac467aa95f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-37077" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x, y) = (x + y^{2})^{2}$ at the point $A(-1,-2)$ in the direction towards the point $B(2, 2)$." :question/worked-solution "The direction from $A$ to $B$ is $\\langle3,4\\rangle$, with unit vector $u=\\langle3,4\\rangle/5$. Since $\\nabla f=\\langle2(x+y^2),4y(x+y^2)\\rangle$, we have $\\nabla f(-1,-2)=\\langle6,-24\\rangle$. Therefore $$D_uf=\\frac{18-96}{5}=-\\frac{78}{5}.$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235525 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7eaac021-36b6-54cc-b7ec-c212007fad51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7eaac021-36b6-54cc-b7ec-c212007fad51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234738} :answer-field/id #uuid "61ede809-36cc-5d59-b1d8-f7a0b29d9d5f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235075}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e02c41aa-7da1-51d0-a8bf-4d3360c07bca" :question/math-academy-id "q-168116" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=\\text{div}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{V}$ at the point $(1,1)$ in the direction of the vector $\\mathbf{v}=-3\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+4\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \nThe required directional derivative is ${f}_{\\mathbf{u}}^{'}(1,1)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n{{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{\\mathbf{u}}^{'}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\mathbf{u}}^{'}(a,b)=\\mathrm{∇}f(a,b)\\cdot \\mathbf{u}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{u}$ is a unit vector in the direction of $\\mathbf{v}.$\n\nFirst, we find the unit vector $\\mathbf{u}$ in the direction of $\\mathbf{v}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖\\mathbf{v}‖ & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{4}^{2}}=\\sqrt{25}=5 \\\\ \\mathbf{u} & =\\frac{1}{5}(-3\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+4\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn part 3, we found that the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\mathrm{∇}\\hspace{-0.167em}f(1,1)=\\mathrm{∇}(\\text{div}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{V})\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{(1,\\hspace{0.167em}1)}=4\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\mathbf{u}}^{'}(1,1) & =\\mathrm{∇}\\hspace{-0.167em}f(1,1)\\cdot \\mathbf{u} \\\\  & =(4\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j})\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}(-3\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+4\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j})) \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 4}{5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265867 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08151725-c767-5bfa-8cc0-566dac73c7c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+2}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263073} {:answer/id #uuid "6b75a71e-ff62-5063-9c04-4318296a44fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263928} {:answer/id #uuid "8f591e1b-9777-5d0f-b497-43f656adfa40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+4}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264230} {:answer/id #uuid "bd6ad8b4-a673-5008-ae07-fbef7600a1fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264645} {:answer/id #uuid "bd888fe4-7f5e-51b1-a53d-363189aedc9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08151725-c767-5bfa-8cc0-566dac73c7c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+2}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263073} :answer-field/id #uuid "93ddfe34-8e2a-5c0d-ad1d-5d50a7d04569" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265512}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5e9cc9e7-1d62-51d1-8fa2-dd51fa7daa28" :question/math-academy-id "q-130257" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=xy$ at the point $(2,1)$ in the direction of the vector $\\mathbf{v}=\\sqrt{3}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}.$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{\\mathbf{u}}^{'}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\mathbf{u}}^{'}(a,b)=\\mathrm{∇}f(a,b)\\cdot \\mathbf{u}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{u}$ is a unit vector in the direction of $\\mathbf{v}.$\n\nFirst, we find the unit vector $\\mathbf{u}$ in the direction of $\\mathbf{v}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖\\mathbf{v}‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{1}^{2}}=2 \\\\ \\mathbf{u} & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(2,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathrm{∇}\\hspace{-0.167em}f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)\\text{ }\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)\\text{ }\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+x\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\ \\mathrm{∇}\\hspace{-0.167em}f(2,1) & =\\mathbf{i}+2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\mathbf{u}}^{'}(2,1) & =\\mathrm{∇}\\hspace{-0.167em}f(2,1)\\cdot \\mathbf{u} \\\\  & =(\\mathbf{i}+2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1(\\sqrt{3})+2(1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+2}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265868 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1da1714c-2291-5808-ac0e-0808ab462f8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263272} {:answer/id #uuid "450b63f8-2ed8-5c35-8a78-b5c67477b5ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263607} {:answer/id #uuid "72992976-c623-506b-9f6f-3a6145bc7b3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263992} {:answer/id #uuid "7dc54a79-4160-5b82-ac56-cae08fe005df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264084} {:answer/id #uuid "b7690e09-485b-5e3c-b1cf-05000b42442a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72992976-c623-506b-9f6f-3a6145bc7b3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263992} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c8b53a4-366c-5e74-a168-e6f6544ed5ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265461}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "35885778-6551-5cbf-9f14-c659423ae334" :question/math-academy-id "q-130260" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})$ at the point $(0,-1)$ in the direction of the vector $\\mathbf{v}=3\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+4\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{\\mathbf{u}}^{'}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\mathbf{u}}^{'}(a,b)=\\mathrm{∇}f(a,b)\\cdot \\mathbf{u}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{u}$ is a unit vector in the direction of $\\mathbf{v}.$\n\nFirst, we find the unit vector $\\mathbf{u}$ in the direction of $\\mathbf{v}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖\\mathbf{v}‖ & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}=5 \\\\ \\mathbf{u} & =\\frac{1}{5}(3\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+4\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(0,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathrm{∇}\\hspace{-0.167em}f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}))\\text{ }\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}))\\text{ }\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\mathbf{j} \\\\ \\mathrm{∇}\\hspace{-0.167em}f(0,-1) & =\\frac{2(0)}{{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{2(-1)}{{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =-2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\mathbf{u}}^{'}(0,-1) & =\\mathrm{∇}\\hspace{-0.167em}f(0,-1)\\cdot \\mathbf{u} \\\\  & =-2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}(3\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+4\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2(4)}{5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265869 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "086fecd5-a126-5f32-9308-1bc895c050b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263080} {:answer/id #uuid "8d43de9a-94e9-5878-939e-2733944f61c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264208} {:answer/id #uuid "9b78ab4c-27f6-5a87-8918-b6215e38243b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264329} {:answer/id #uuid "b92952ce-92d6-5fe1-84dc-4e5ec973c535" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264605} {:answer/id #uuid "cd1aafca-14b7-5d95-9816-988f20570192" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b78ab4c-27f6-5a87-8918-b6215e38243b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264329} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e1d9c83-156f-56e6-8ce6-3d01bf086064" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265433}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae068a0a-3a23-5516-a4b7-13c70903e5db" :question/math-academy-id "q-130263" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-xy$ at the point $(1,1)$ in the direction of the vector $\\mathbf{v}=\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{j}.$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{\\mathbf{u}}^{'}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\mathbf{u}}^{'}(a,b)=\\mathrm{∇}f(a,b)\\cdot \\mathbf{u}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{u}$ is a unit vector in the direction of $\\mathbf{v}.$\n\nFirst, we find the unit vector $\\mathbf{u}$ in the direction of $\\mathbf{v}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖\\mathbf{v}‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\mathbf{u} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{j})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathrm{∇}\\hspace{-0.167em}f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-xy)\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-xy)\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =(2x-y)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(2y-x)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\ \\mathrm{∇}\\hspace{-0.167em}f(1,1) & =(2(1)-1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(2(1)-1)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\mathbf{u}}^{'}(1,1) & =\\mathrm{∇}\\hspace{-0.167em}f(1,1)\\cdot \\mathbf{u} \\\\  & =(\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\mathbf{i}-\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1(1)+1(-1)}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323790 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00835dd1-8061-59e4-8040-48a957847175" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321154} {:answer/id #uuid "2b84de9a-1d96-5d76-b304-fcc568ae08c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321481} {:answer/id #uuid "8f8d9dd6-ab7c-531c-92df-429bb88b6255" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322286} {:answer/id #uuid "93873ce7-adfb-5826-85f5-744afae73ad2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322319} {:answer/id #uuid "f4e6066c-22d2-5127-a385-fb4a7da7ae82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4e6066c-22d2-5127-a385-fb4a7da7ae82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323067} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2ab9660-72ee-5cec-b767-3be5f30759da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323617}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0cd131d3-dbf5-532a-a1c1-f69d113636a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-36290" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y}+{x}^{2}y$ at the point $A(1,0)$ in the direction towards the point $B(0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{\\mathbf{u}}^{'}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\mathbf{u}}^{'}(a,b)=\\mathrm{∇}f(a,b)\\cdot \\mathbf{u}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{u}$ is a unit vector in the direction of $\\mathbf{v}.$\n\nFirst, we find the direction vector and the corresponding unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨0,1⟩-⟨1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,1⟩ \\\\ \\mathbf{u} & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}}{‖\\overset{\\to }{AB}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}}⟨-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $A(1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{y}+{x}^{2}y),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{y}+{x}^{2}y)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{y}+2xy,\\,x{e}^{y}+{x}^{2}⟩ \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,0) & =⟨{e}^{0}+2\\cdot 1\\cdot 0,\\,1\\cdot {e}^{0}+{1}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\mathbf{u}}^{'}(1,0) & =\\mathrm{∇}f(1,0)\\cdot \\mathbf{u} \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}2⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354470 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1304514c-b435-522f-ad3a-591f2559a22b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11\\sqrt{34}}{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351730} {:answer/id #uuid "7e4fba7a-fe7c-5a9c-9fbe-87782d23df70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11\\sqrt{43}}{43}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352676} {:answer/id #uuid "c8a1b502-7fbf-5960-aaec-5f60565ea22e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10\\sqrt{34}}{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353314} {:answer/id #uuid "c94460ac-494e-513e-82ed-c599cb03d029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10\\sqrt{43}}{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353320} {:answer/id #uuid "f1e9e528-e824-57bb-899a-9e75210a8db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8a1b502-7fbf-5960-aaec-5f60565ea22e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10\\sqrt{34}}{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353314} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9f8833b-3f19-5c49-a196-1b1b54521800" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354216}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f8f45df0-069c-5e4a-a4d7-bdd2e15f5467" :question/math-academy-id "q-86429" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=6{x}^{2}+2y$ at the point $(0,1)$ in the direction of the vector $\\mathbf{v}=3\\mathbf{i}+5\\mathbf{j}.$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{\\mathbf{u}}^{'}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\mathbf{u}}^{'}(a,b)=\\mathrm{∇}f(a,b)\\cdot \\mathbf{u}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{u}$ is a unit vector in the direction of $\\mathbf{v}.$\n\nFirst, we find the unit vector $\\mathbf{u}$ in the direction of $\\mathbf{v}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖\\mathbf{v}‖ & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{5}^{2}}=\\sqrt{34} \\\\ \\mathbf{u} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{34}}(3\\mathbf{i}+5\\mathbf{j})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathrm{∇}\\hspace{-0.167em}f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6{x}^{2}+2y)\\text{ }\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(6{x}^{2}+2y)\\text{ }\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =12x\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\ \\mathrm{∇}\\hspace{-0.167em}f(0,1) & =(12\\cdot 0)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+2\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =2\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\mathbf{u}}^{'}(0,1) & =\\mathrm{∇}\\hspace{-0.167em}f(0,1)\\cdot \\mathbf{u} \\\\  & =2\\mathbf{j}\\cdot (\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{34}}\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{34}}\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 5}{\\sqrt{34}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\sqrt{34}}{34}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446241 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d2f5038-f42a-5fd7-a95d-a297da774c15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446193} {:answer/id #uuid "a9d07651-85d5-5624-ae13-7a41e816c585" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446216} {:answer/id #uuid "b248e7e5-413b-5466-b7ed-293308db0e18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446218} {:answer/id #uuid "d058285d-919c-56d4-bc37-2e175c0f050a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446225} {:answer/id #uuid "eb4ac023-e663-5e98-b2d3-aa3c2ec67064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446228}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d058285d-919c-56d4-bc37-2e175c0f050a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446225} :answer-field/id #uuid "cea3cee4-a045-5dc7-8596-6cf26a0cb161" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446236}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4c3374df-275b-5fb9-8864-40efeec8b5b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-36306" :question/problem "Given the function  $g(x,y)=({x}^{2}+y)^{2}$, find its directional derivative at the\npoint $A(-1,1)$ in the direction that's towards the point $B(3,4).$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $v$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)=∇f(a,b)\\cdot u\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is a unit vector in the direction of $v.$\n\nFirst, we find the direction vector and the corresponding unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨3,4⟩-⟨-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,3⟩ \\\\ u & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}}{‖\\overset{\\to }{AB}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}}⟨4,3⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨4,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the gradient $∇g(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $A(-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+y)^{2},\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+y)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4x({x}^{2}+y),\\,2({x}^{2}+y)⟩ \\\\ ∇g(-1,1) & =⟨4\\cdot (-1)\\cdot ((-1)^{2}+1),2\\cdot ((-1)^{2}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{u}^{′}(-1,1) & =∇g(-1,1)\\cdot u \\\\  & =⟨-8,4⟩\\cdot ⟨\\frac{4}{5},\\frac{3}{5}⟩ \\\\  & =-8\\cdot \\frac{4}{5}+4\\cdot \\frac{3}{5} \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446242 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "021bf1f8-b881-536a-a8f1-f59bbd10c0cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{5\\sqrt{13}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446176} {:answer/id #uuid "455dead3-5a38-5f75-bb6f-3603611372d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446188} {:answer/id #uuid "502f0fe4-aa68-585a-bbd4-188d4c9372d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446195} {:answer/id #uuid "5d9b9f76-b123-5719-bc4e-29ca3f63e30e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446197} {:answer/id #uuid "b8aca910-6177-50b0-976d-f5a0cad4d3f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446220}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "021bf1f8-b881-536a-a8f1-f59bbd10c0cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{5\\sqrt{13}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446176} :answer-field/id #uuid "be838696-b1cd-5c8f-81ac-b0d86172dd65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446235}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5fc2a3e0-1de4-50ca-b644-c592b3edb577" :question/math-academy-id "q-130268" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ at the point $A(4,3)$ in the direction towards the point $B(1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $v$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)=∇f(a,b)\\cdot u\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is a unit vector in the direction of $v.$\n\nFirst, we find the direction vector and the corresponding unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,1⟩-⟨4,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-2⟩ \\\\ u & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}}{‖\\overset{\\to }{AB}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}}⟨-3,-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}⟨-3,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $A(4,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}},\\,\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}⟩ \\\\ ∇f(4,3) & =⟨\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{3}^{2}}},\\,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{3}^{2}}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{4}{5},\\frac{3}{5}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{u}^{′}(4,3) & =∇f(4,3)\\cdot u \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{4}{5},\\frac{3}{5}⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}},-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{4(-3)+3(-2)}{5\\sqrt{13}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{18}{5\\sqrt{13}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518124 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05e252ff-bff2-5a0c-8722-678c22a7c16c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517501} {:answer/id #uuid "070f81d7-bbdd-59f5-971a-c1e85fd656fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{10}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517503} {:answer/id #uuid "3a8dff85-9179-52c1-a1eb-e2b80b8d392e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\sqrt{10}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517603} {:answer/id #uuid "636cdbc8-2c6a-553b-a040-1b1eb24c4aed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517671} {:answer/id #uuid "9a89bbd5-05e0-5b9e-875f-8fbff4dcb441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6\\sqrt{10}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a89bbd5-05e0-5b9e-875f-8fbff4dcb441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6\\sqrt{10}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517783} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa6bc3a1-b754-5de6-a15a-17b5690dd1bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518094}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "36bc1d86-9d95-5fad-8592-9df3687ca62a" :question/math-academy-id "q-86533" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=(2{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2})^{2}$ at the point $A(-1,-1)$ in the direction towards the point $B(2,0).$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $v$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)=∇f(a,b)\\cdot u\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is a unit vector in the direction of $v.$\n\nFirst, we find the direction vector and the corresponding unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨2,0⟩-⟨-1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,1⟩ \\\\ u & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}}{‖\\overset{\\to }{AB}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}}}⟨3,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨3,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $A(-1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2})^{2},\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2})^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8x(2{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}),\\,36{y}^{3}-24{x}^{2}y⟩ \\\\ ∇f(-1,-1) & =⟨8(-1)\\cdot (2(-1)^{2}-3(-1)^{2}),36(-1)^{3}-24(-1)^{2}(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,-12⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{u}^{′}(-1,-1) & =∇f(-1,-1)\\cdot u \\\\  & =⟨8,-12⟩\\cdot ⟨\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}},\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟩ \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}-12\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\sqrt{10}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548195 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0819b00b-ddf8-51fd-b337-f67bbb68e05a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24 \\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548189} {:answer/id #uuid "2d2d0946-fae9-532f-80d5-010b263a3d4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548190} {:answer/id #uuid "66c7d9c2-81ae-5068-8c96-91f51d97a8ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548191} {:answer/id #uuid "895ba611-f922-55ef-9624-62e08b1e4ef5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{16 \\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548193} {:answer/id #uuid "c4eef04d-da15-5f2a-aac3-6cfce868c8fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0819b00b-ddf8-51fd-b337-f67bbb68e05a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24 \\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548189} :answer-field/id #uuid "70e128fd-ce69-5958-8d26-3af81c7ff0b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548192}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e4d2c788-fb3a-5910-a90d-014c2de97596" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=4 x^{2} y + 2 x e^{y}$ at the point $A(2,0)$ in the direction towards the point $B(4,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $v$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)=∇f(a,b)\\cdot u\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is a unit vector in the direction of $v.$\n\nFirst, we find the direction vector and the corresponding unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨4,1⟩-⟨2,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1⟩ \\\\ u & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}}{‖\\overset{\\to }{AB}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(1)^{2}}}⟨2,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $A(2,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4 x^{2} y + 2 x e^{y}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4 x^{2} y + 2 x e^{y})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8 x y + 2 e^{y},2 x \\left(2 x + e^{y}\\right)⟩ \\\\ ∇f(2,0) & =⟨8 (2) (0) + 2 e^{(0)},4 (2)^{2} + 2 (2) e^{(0)}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,20⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{u}^{′}(2,0) & =∇f(2,0)\\cdot u \\\\  & =⟨2,20⟩\\cdot ⟨\\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5},\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{24 \\sqrt{5}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563741 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00433fb2-2689-50b6-b5ae-b3213b484e7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562937} {:answer/id #uuid "81f0d8bc-19f0-5e3d-ad6f-8e1c66829afd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563232} {:answer/id #uuid "bc4239ca-8453-592c-a801-dc055bf9ad37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563360} {:answer/id #uuid "c97f5424-984d-5602-8981-349f5455aec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563389} {:answer/id #uuid "da9987fb-7331-55ac-8916-60a446822552" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da9987fb-7331-55ac-8916-60a446822552" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563423} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa2be9cd-8e25-5c22-a57c-dbf36efef798" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563612}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d5075c32-f624-572f-a2d3-78616466d14e" :question/math-academy-id "q-86430" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=(2{x}^{2}-y)^{2}$ at the point $A(-1,1)$ in the direction towards the point $B(-2,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $v$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)=∇f(a,b)\\cdot u\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is a unit vector in the direction of $v.$\n\nFirst, we find the direction vector and the corresponding unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨-2,2⟩-⟨-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,1⟩ \\\\ u & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}}{‖\\overset{\\to }{AB}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}}⟨-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $A(-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}-y)^{2},\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}-y)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨16{x}^{3}-8xy,\\,2y-4{x}^{2}⟩ \\\\ ∇f(-1,1) & =⟨16(-1)^{3}-8(-1)(1),\\,2(1)-4(-1)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{u}^{′}(-1,1) & =∇f(-1,1)\\cdot u \\\\  & =⟨-8,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =(-8)\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)-2\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563750 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04dcdfb7-813c-5013-92a6-1f6a2e40d34a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562947} {:answer/id #uuid "3293ed3c-f84a-5bdd-b26a-c1ac19d7d55f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563059} {:answer/id #uuid "6635b13b-ede2-5436-984d-23828cf04773" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563181} {:answer/id #uuid "7d25f5da-9280-508e-a834-dd75fe932211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563220} {:answer/id #uuid "992d4136-ab07-5324-b78a-7177af5b18ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3293ed3c-f84a-5bdd-b26a-c1ac19d7d55f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563059} :answer-field/id #uuid "235850d9-4b74-5c62-9d1d-41026c4c9828" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563542}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "df6440e4-6b40-5b4e-87c9-62e58eb89d0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130258" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-6xy+{y}^{2}$ at the point $(-1,3)$ in the direction of the vector $\\mathbf{v}=\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}.$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $v$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)=∇f(a,b)\\cdot u\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is a unit vector in the direction of $v.$\n\nFirst, we find the unit vector $u$ in the direction of $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ u & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(i+j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(-1,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-6xy+{y}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-6xy+{y}^{2})\\text{ }j \\\\  & =(2x-6y)\\,i+(2y-6x)j \\\\ ∇\\,f(-1,3) & =(2(-1)-6(3))\\,i+(2(3)-6(-1))j \\\\  & =-20\\,i+12\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{u}^{′}(-1,3) & =∇\\,f(-1,3)\\cdot u \\\\  & =(-20\\,i+12\\,j)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(i+j) \\\\  & =\\frac{-20(1)+12(1)}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563760 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c8383c9-5a00-5106-8ade-ebcb1afc1644" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562966} {:answer/id #uuid "2ea52a0e-e6a5-522f-8a2f-e28cb7fa9518" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563050} {:answer/id #uuid "48b88652-e6ed-5cdf-94e0-9c52630df3e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563105} {:answer/id #uuid "68b0f87b-d56a-5e56-bcb2-6c135e0e44a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563187} {:answer/id #uuid "804a3d7f-93d1-5460-9e8a-4cea93ac58d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ea52a0e-e6a5-522f-8a2f-e28cb7fa9518" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563050} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f6b8a55-8b0f-5157-98ff-b7ec894bdaee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563567}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f7872fd6-9c54-5e48-b08b-71d8ca0a2063" :question/math-academy-id "q-83552" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ at the point $(1,1)$ in the direction of the vector $\\mathbf{v}=2\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}.$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $v$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)=∇f(a,b)\\cdot u\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is a unit vector in the direction of $v.$\n\nFirst, we find the unit vector $u$ in the direction of $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}=\\sqrt{5} \\\\ u & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}(2i+j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+\\frac{y}{x})\\,i+(\\frac{x}{y}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\,j \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1) & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+\\frac{1}{1})\\,i+(\\frac{1}{1}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)\\,j \\\\  & =i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{u}^{′}(1,1) & =∇\\,f(1,1)\\cdot u \\\\  & =(i+j)\\cdot (\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186653564 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04d46f58-6728-5d7e-af77-e0a58bbd497a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653091} {:answer/id #uuid "72fac567-96ad-5cec-a3ac-c6e988127006" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653248} {:answer/id #uuid "76c5d9e8-bbde-5c77-a47f-279b3794c0f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653253} {:answer/id #uuid "a3fc4a80-b819-5043-a846-0e7d55902058" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653308} {:answer/id #uuid "fa361707-efb1-59da-a591-2a5a003acd22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3fc4a80-b819-5043-a846-0e7d55902058" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653308} :answer-field/id #uuid "0972614c-21d4-598f-8522-bcb2bc2b9874" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653446}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6ef219b5-1e6d-577f-990a-3bfd77335bcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-130267" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$ at the point $A(1,e)$ in the direction towards the point $B(-2,e).$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $v$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)=∇f(a,b)\\cdot u\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is a unit vector in the direction of $v.$\n\nFirst, we find the direction vector and the corresponding unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨-2,e⟩-⟨1,e⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,0⟩ \\\\ u & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}}{‖\\overset{\\to }{AB}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}}}⟨-3,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨-3,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $A(1,e):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{ln}⁡y,\\,\\frac{2x}{y}⟩ \\\\ ∇f(1,e) & =⟨2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e,\\,\\frac{2(1)}{e}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\frac{2}{e}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{u}^{′}(1,e) & =∇f(1,e)\\cdot u \\\\  & =⟨2,\\frac{2}{e}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =2(-1)+\\frac{2}{e}(0) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725116 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49a2c2f3-d8a8-5d8a-8fb7-c07f95e2fa18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725107} {:answer/id #uuid "5027ab94-0251-551e-89f5-7fa970132140" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725108} {:answer/id #uuid "5036ff67-7bdc-56ea-a39e-86726cc0abd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725109} {:answer/id #uuid "5254616d-9668-503f-bb2e-845c94341c9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{28}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725111} {:answer/id #uuid "b1c28309-ca10-54c7-b644-8a8c48916fc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5036ff67-7bdc-56ea-a39e-86726cc0abd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725109} :answer-field/id #uuid "eed5dc07-fb31-5332-8176-261ba7d2a2ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725119}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c296adb0-2561-528e-9e42-a549b25c773d" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $g(x,y)=(x^2+y)^2$ at the point $A(1,-2)$ in the direction towards the point $B(-2,2)$." :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative at a point $A$ in the direction of a nonzero vector $\\mathbf v$ is\n\n$$\nD_{\\mathbf u}g(A)=\\nabla g(A)\\cdot\\mathbf u,\n\\qquad \\mathbf u=\\frac{\\mathbf v}{\\|\\mathbf v\\|}.\n$$\n\nThe direction must be represented by a unit vector.\n\nThe direction is from $A$ towards $B$, so subtract the coordinates in that order and normalize:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf v&=\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\langle -2-1,2-(-2)\\rangle=\\langle -3,4\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf v\\|&=\\sqrt{(-3)^2+4^2}=5,\\\\\n\\mathbf u&=\\left\\langle -\\frac{3}{5},\\frac{4}{5}\\right\\rangle.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the chain rule to both partial derivatives, then evaluate at $A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ng_x(x,y)&=2(x^2+y)(2x)=4x(x^2+y),\\\\\ng_y(x,y)&=2(x^2+y),\\\\\n\\nabla g(1,-2)&=\\langle 4(1)(1-2),2(1-2)\\rangle\\\\\n&=\\langle -4,-2\\rangle.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD_{\\mathbf u}g(1,-2)&=\\langle -4,-2\\rangle\\cdot\\left\\langle -\\frac{3}{5},\\frac{4}{5}\\right\\rangle\\\\\n&=\\frac{(-4)(-3)+(-2)(4)}{5}\\\\\n&=\\frac{12-8}{5}=\\frac{4}{5}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725117 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0afc0811-7274-57fb-a09d-67c8f70199a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725104} {:answer/id #uuid "7133a94d-8fea-58d8-a15b-c945b0cdf20a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725112} {:answer/id #uuid "7d6f4edf-5123-5d48-96ad-10cd27b144ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725113} {:answer/id #uuid "bae7b90b-5d8c-5377-b195-26724808f7be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725115} {:answer/id #uuid "fafb5ad3-faa4-5e50-838b-4b665f79bece" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7133a94d-8fea-58d8-a15b-c945b0cdf20a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725112} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f25c80d-3f1f-5a9b-a169-383d56430fe9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725106}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d61f7599-aa77-51db-b099-2ccf964dc7ff" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=x^2+2xy$ at the point $(1,2)$ in the direction of the vector $\\mathbf v=2\\mathbf i-\\mathbf j$." :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative at a point $A$ in the direction of a nonzero vector $\\mathbf v$ is\n\n$$\nD_{\\mathbf u}f(A)=\\nabla f(A)\\cdot\\mathbf u,\n\\qquad \\mathbf u=\\frac{\\mathbf v}{\\|\\mathbf v\\|}.\n$$\n\nThe direction must be represented by a unit vector.\n\nFirst, normalize the supplied direction vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\|\\mathbf v\\|&=\\sqrt{2^2+(-1)^2}=\\sqrt{5},\\\\\n\\mathbf u&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\langle 2,-1\\rangle.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow compute the partial derivatives and evaluate the gradient at $(1,2)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(x,y)&=2x+2y,\\\\\nf_y(x,y)&=2x,\\\\\n\\nabla f(1,2)&=\\langle 2(1)+2(2),2(1)\\rangle=\\langle 6,2\\rangle.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTaking the dot product gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD_{\\mathbf u}f(1,2)&=\\langle 6,2\\rangle\\cdot\\frac{\\langle 2,-1\\rangle}{\\sqrt{5}}\\\\\n&=\\frac{6(2)+2(-1)}{\\sqrt{5}}\\\\\n&=\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5}}=2\\sqrt{5}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725118 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2efddd40-658d-5fa2-8f0a-037d5f305c8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15\\sqrt{13}}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2efddd40-658d-5fa2-8f0a-037d5f305c8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15\\sqrt{13}}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725105} :answer-field/id #uuid "5079543a-73a4-522d-806d-3d04ff473efb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186725110}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d8cdb080-bad0-522b-9483-8dec1e7ba322" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $h(x,y)=\\dfrac{x^2+y}{x-y}$ at the point $A(2,1)$ in the direction towards the point $B(-1,3)$.\n\nThe required directional derivative is {{field-1}}. Give an exact value." :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative at a point $A$ in the direction of a nonzero vector $\\mathbf v$ is\n\n$$\nD_{\\mathbf u}h(A)=\\nabla h(A)\\cdot\\mathbf u,\n\\qquad \\mathbf u=\\frac{\\mathbf v}{\\|\\mathbf v\\|}.\n$$\n\nThe direction must be represented by a unit vector.\n\nFirst find the direction from $A$ towards $B$ and its unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf v&=\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\langle -1-2,3-1\\rangle=\\langle -3,2\\rangle,\\\\\n\\|\\mathbf v\\|&=\\sqrt{(-3)^2+2^2}=\\sqrt{13},\\\\\n\\mathbf u&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}\\langle -3,2\\rangle.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $2-1=1\\ne 0$, the function is differentiable near $A$. Use the quotient rule for each partial derivative. In the $y$ derivative, the derivative of the denominator $x-y$ is $-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nh_x(x,y)&=\\frac{2x(x-y)-(x^2+y)}{(x-y)^2},\\\\\nh_y(x,y)&=\\frac{(x-y)+(x^2+y)}{(x-y)^2},\\\\\nh_x(2,1)&=\\frac{4(1)-5}{1^2}=-1,\\\\\nh_y(2,1)&=\\frac{1+5}{1^2}=6.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the gradient at the starting point $A$, then take the dot product with the unit direction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nD_{\\mathbf u}h(2,1)&=\\langle -1,6\\rangle\\cdot\\frac{\\langle -3,2\\rangle}{\\sqrt{13}}\\\\\n&=\\frac{(-1)(-3)+6(2)}{\\sqrt{13}}\\\\\n&=\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{13}}=\\frac{15\\sqrt{13}}{13}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Directional Derivative"}]}
